WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:04.313
Two baseball players stood in the Metro City Stadium parking lot.

2
00:00:04.314 --> 00:00:07.016
"Big game tomorrow, Dale," one player said.

3
00:00:07.017 --> 00:00:09.573
"It'll be our first game without Hitz."

4
00:00:09.574 --> 00:00:13.615
"Good," Dale said. "He's a bad sport.

5
00:00:13.616 --> 00:00:16.969
He kept inventing equipment to help him cheat."

6
00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:18.484
Manny nodded.

7
00:00:18.485 --> 00:00:21.232
"I remember when he had that weird baseball.

8
00:00:21.233 --> 00:00:23.821
He could make it explode."

9
00:00:23.822 --> 00:00:25.601
Dale shook his head.

10
00:00:25.602 --> 00:00:30.908
"I'm glad Coach Biggs kicked him off the team. See you tomorrow, Manny!"

11
00:00:30.909 --> 00:00:33.820
Just then a dark shadow covered the parking lot.

12
00:00:33.821 --> 00:00:36.029
The players looked up.

13
00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:40.923
Dale gulped. "What is that?"

14
00:00:40.924 --> 00:00:45.320
*** "Another run!" Terrell said. "This is

15
00:00:45.321 --> 00:00:48.964
awful." Roxy and her friends were at Metro City

16
00:00:48.965 --> 00:00:52.337
Stadium. The Metro City Miners were playing the Lumbertown

17
00:00:52.338 --> 00:00:57.158
Loggers. The Miners' pitcher threw the

18
00:00:57.159 --> 00:00:59.935
baseball. The batter swung.

19
00:00:59.936 --> 00:01:05.298
Crack! The ball landed in the

20
00:01:05.299 --> 00:01:08.987
stands. "Home run for the Loggers!" the announcer

21
00:01:08.988 --> 00:01:14.387
said. Roxy groaned. "The Miners' pitcher is

22
00:01:14.388 --> 00:01:17.239
terrible. The Loggers have three runs

23
00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:20.825
already." "I can't believe Dale Rivers isn't here," Jack

24
00:01:20.826 --> 00:01:22.763
said. "He's our star

25
00:01:22.764 --> 00:01:25.311
pitcher!" The pitcher threw

26
00:01:25.312 --> 00:01:30.988
again. The batter swung and then ran to first

27
00:01:30.989 --> 00:01:38.623
base. Two more batters got onto

28
00:01:38.624 --> 00:01:43.778
bases. "Bases loaded!" the announcer

29
00:01:43.779 --> 00:01:49.585
said. The next batter sent the ball far into the

30
00:01:49.586 --> 00:01:54.810
stands. "That's a grand slam for the Loggers!" the announcer said.

31
00:01:54.811 --> 00:01:58.016
"No!" Mara cried.

32
00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:02.323
"The Loggers are winning, seven to nothing!"

33
00:02:02.324 --> 00:02:06.434
Jack sighed. "We'll never catch up.

34
00:02:06.435 --> 00:02:08.337
Manny Gomez isn't here.

35
00:02:08.338 --> 00:02:11.389
He's the Miners' best home run hitter."

36
00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:15.336
Another Loggers player was soon on second base.

37
00:02:15.337 --> 00:02:18.645
"I wish Rocket Girl could help," Jack said.

38
00:02:18.646 --> 00:02:25.504
"If she played for the Miners, she'd get a million home runs!"

39
00:02:25.505 --> 00:02:31.957
Terrell covered his face and moaned. "This is a really bad game."

40
00:02:31.958 --> 00:02:36.482
Mara's stomach grumbled. "I'm hungry."

41
00:02:36.483 --> 00:02:38.589
She looked over her shoulder.

42
00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:41.645
A snack bar was at the top of the steps.

43
00:02:41.646 --> 00:02:45.206
"But I don't want to miss any of the game."

44
00:02:45.207 --> 00:02:46.758
Terrell looked up.

45
00:02:46.759 --> 00:02:50.562
"You can't get up while the Miners are pitching! It's bad luck!"

46
00:02:50.563 --> 00:02:53.326
"I know!" Mara said.

47
00:02:53.327 --> 00:02:58.596
Roxy grinned. "It's too bad Rocket Girl can't get a snack for you."

48
00:02:58.597 --> 00:03:02.589
"Ha-ha." Mara pretended to laugh.

49
00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:07.168
Roxy's watch beeped.

50
00:03:07.169 --> 00:03:11.924
"Mayor Bloom," she whispered. "Is everything okay?"

51
00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:13.661
The mayor looked worried.

52
00:03:13.662 --> 00:03:17.336
"Rocket Girl, I need you to go to Police Headquarters.

53
00:03:17.337 --> 00:03:22.014
Two Miners players disappeared. No one can find them."

54
00:03:22.015 --> 00:03:25.025
"Oh no," Roxy whispered.

55
00:03:25.026 --> 00:03:28.665
"You mean Dale Rivers and Manny Gomez, right?"

56
00:03:28.666 --> 00:03:30.849
Mayor Bloom nodded.

57
00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:33.499
"Don't worry, Mayor," Roxy said.

58
00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:37.592
"I'll find them."

